\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl202\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .   Not what these hands have done
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Can save this guilty soul;
\par  Not what this toiling flesh has borne
\par  Can make my spirit whole.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   Not what I feel or do\tab 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj  Can give me peace with God;
\par  Not all my prayers, and sighs and tears
\par Can bear my awful load.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.   Thy work alone, O Christ,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Can ease this weight of sin;
\par  Thy blood alone, O Lamb of God,
\par  Can give within me peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Thy love to me,O God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Not mine, O Lord, to Thee,
\par Can rid me of this dark unrest,
\par And set my spirit free.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.    Thy grace alone, O God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 To me can pardon speak;
\par Thy power alone, O Son of God,
\par Can this sore bondage break.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  I bless the Christ of God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I rest on Love divine,
\par And with unfaltering lip and heart,
\par \pard       I call this Saviour mine.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

